# Findings gitleaks must not fail on, one fingerprint per line.
#
# CI scans a COMMIT RANGE, not the working tree (see .github/workflows/ci.yml), so it
# re-reads historical diffs. A false positive that has already been corrected in the tree
# is still present in the commit that introduced it, and reappears as soon as a wider
# range is scanned — which is exactly what happens when `development` is promoted to
# `main` and the range spans every commit since the last release.
#
# Exempt individual findings by fingerprint only. Never disable a rule or exclude a path:
# a path exclusion silently covers every future secret committed there, a fingerprint
# covers one line of one commit.

